## The one thing you should know

**The draft's typing tiebreaker was an unverifiable quote.** The 2022 line — *"Being scared to fully correct yourself so that there's no more pain to talk about, that definitely scares me"* — was the hinge the whole Type 4 argument swung on, and fresh eyes praised it as the strongest structural move in the piece. Eight targeted searches turned up nothing, and the create-stage log carries no citation either. It's gone.

I rebuilt the tiebreaker on material that checks out: **December 2023, thirteen six-hour sessions, most of his body blacked out in solid ink**, revealed February 20 2024 captioned "for spiritual purposes only," and the next day's lyric — *"I had a breakdown and tatted my entire body except one line."* An Achiever doesn't destroy the merchandise, and a man who wanted rid of the old version would have finished the job. Stronger than what it replaced, and sourced.

## Other substantive changes

- **The confession is now pressure-tested in the body.** "I got to ruin everything" was said on a promo podcast, mid-cycle, about the cycle — the kindest possible account of a rehab stay and a broken engagement. The answer is the calendar: the confession is a year old, the behavior is twenty.
- **Fox section fills its four-year hole** — her November 2023 disclosure of the miscarriage, his February 2024 answer on record, the separation. It now says what the job cost and how it ended.
- **Generational spine closed** — Casie (b. 2009, he was nineteen) as the third nine-year-old, with her August 2025 People "big advisor" quote. A man whose method is self-sabotage runs decisions past a teenager who stops him.
